message: "If you use this research package, please cite it as below."
title: "Privacy by Request: Immigrant Settlement and the Limits of Individual Control in the Data Broker Economy (research package)"
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-10-28
authors:
  - family-names: Chala
    given-names: Endalkachew H.
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6210-6706
    affiliation: "Center for an Informed Public, University of Washington"
repository-code: https://github.com/Endalk-Chala/privacy-by-request
license: MIT
keywords:
  - data brokers
  - people-search sites
  - privacy
  - immigrants
  - contextual integrity
  - mixed methods
  - Minnesota
abstract: >-
  Protocol, instruments, codebook, synthetic data and analysis code for a mixed-methods study of
  data-broker exposure among immigrant adults in the Twin Cities, Minnesota. The study measures
  findability on six consumer people-search sites (six sites by seven fields, scored 0 to 2),
  compares it with participants' pre-lookup expectations and awareness, and traces the
  settlement-era disclosures through which exposure is produced.
